# Files the Tauri CLI's dev watcher should NOT rebuild/restart the app for.
# Gitignore syntax, rooted here.
#
# At the REPO ROOT, not in `src-tauri/`, because the dev watcher watches every
# in-workspace path dependency too — `crates/cmdr-index/`, `crates/cmdr-fs/`, and
# anything we add next — and the CLI builds one matcher over the common ancestor
# of all of them. A shield inside `src-tauri/` covers only `src-tauri/`, so a
# colocated doc edit anywhere under `crates/` would restart the app (verified
# 2026-07-31 against `@tauri-apps/cli` 2.11.4: the CLI logged "File
# crates/cmdr-index/CLAUDE.md changed. Rebuilding application..."). Here, every
# watched folder is covered, including the ones that don't exist yet.
#
# The CLI reads this ONCE at watcher startup, so editing it needs a `pnpm dev`
# restart to take effect.

# Colocated agent docs. 150+ CLAUDE.md / DETAILS.md files live next to the code
# they describe, and agents update them constantly alongside it. Without this,
# every one of those edits rebuilds the whole app.
# Verified 2026-06: the watcher logs "File src-tauri/src/mcp/CLAUDE.md changed.
# Rebuilding application..." without this line, and stays quiet with it.
# Vite has its own equivalent shield (`server.watch.ignored` in vite.config.js).
*.md

# Atomic-write temp files (`CLAUDE.md.tmp.<pid>.<hash>`, etc.). Editors and agents
# save via temp+rename, and the `.tmp.<pid>.<hash>` intermediate doesn't end in
# `.md`, so it leaks past the `*.md` shield above and rebuilds the whole app on
# every doc edit. The real file's rename (e.g. → `CLAUDE.md`) still triggers a
# rebuild when it should; only the transient temp is ignored.
*.tmp.*
